 "notes": "28 stations, numbered 4–29 plus 26B and 27B. The list is headed \"EAST OF SCOTLAND.\" (line 531) and split under the sub-headings Shetland, Orkney and Mainland. I put the sub-heading in coast. This list names no keepers and gives no light characters.\n\nHow I read the columns:\n- **other** holds the printed columns from left to right, joined with \"; \": returns in 6 years (left blank for some stations), then value (Roman), then height in feet. For example, \"4; IV.; 230\" means 4 returns in 6 years, value IV., 230 ft. A blank column is left out rather than shown as empty.\n- **marks:** \"*\" is in the \"In 1885\" column and means a return was sent in 1885. \"†\" means a new station, 1885-86, per the footnote at line 574.\n- **name:** I dropped the comma that separates the name from the place.\n- **fragments:** these are whole printed lines, leading spaces kept.\n\nRows to check:\n- **26B, Carr Rock:** printed in italics as \"_Carr Rock Light-ship_\". I split it into name \"Carr Rock\" and type \"Light-ship\", so the italic underscores cover both. Marks are \"italic; †\". It has no returns, no value, and only \"?\" where the value/height would be, so I put \"?\" in other.\n- **27B, Fidra:** the returns column shows \"1st\" instead of a number. I take this to mean its first return, but that is my reading. I put \"1st\" in other. It has no \"*\" in the 1885 column, no value and no height.\n- **9, Start Point:** has \"*\" for 1885 but a blank in the 6-year count.\n\nCopied as printed, but worth a reader's attention:\n- \"Whalsey Skerries\" is usually spelt Whalsay. \"N. Ronaldshay\" and \"N. Unst\" are abbreviated in the print.\n- \"Tarbat Head, East Ross\" is the light usually called Tarbat Ness.\n- \"Chanonry Point, Elgin\": Chanonry Point is on the Black Isle in Ross-shire, not Elgin. The county looks wrong in the print. A recent commit noted a separate Chanonry Point slip in the 1879 list.\n- \"Cromarty, East Cromarty\": the county is printed that way.\n- \"Girdleness\" and \"Montroseness\" are each printed as one word.\n- \"Fife Coast\" for Bell Rock and Carr Rock is a locality, not a county. Bell Rock is really off Angus/Forfar.\n\nThe lead-in line about migration values says \"the the\" (a doubled word in the source). That is outside the rows.",
